-id pub-id-type="pmid">7916056</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Mita</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Morimyo</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Okano</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Koike</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Nohara</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Kwasaki</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Kadono-Okuda</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Yamamoto</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Suzuki</surname><given-names>MG</given-names></name><name><surname>Shimada</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Goldsmith</surname><given-names>MR</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The construction of an EST database for <italic>Bombyx mori</italic> and its application</article-title><source>Proc Natl Acad Sci USA</source><year>2003</year><volume>100</volume><fpage>14121</fpage><lpage>14126</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1073/pnas.2234984100</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Mita K, Morimyo M, Okano K, Koike Y, Nohara J, Kwasaki H, Kadono-Okuda K, Yamamoto K, Suzuki MG, Shimada T, Goldsmith MR (2003) The construction of an EST database for Bombyx mori and its application. Proc Natl Acad Sci USA 100:14121&#x02013;14126 <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14614147</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR15"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Sehnal</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Akai</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Insects silk glands: their types, development and function, and effects of environmental factors and morphogenetic hormones on them</article-title><source>Int J Insect Morphol Embryol</source